n" [:option {:value "2008517"} "Kayak Doubles, 500 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008531"} "Kayak Fours, 500 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008542"} "Canadian Singles, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008559"} "Canadian Doubles, 500 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008572"} "Kayak Singles, 500 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008609"} "Kayak Fours, 500 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008621"} "Canadian Singles, 200 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008638"} "Canadian Doubles, 500 metres, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "255221"} "1960"] "\n" [:option {:value "255282"} "1964"] "\n" [:option {:value "255346"} "1968"] "\n" [:option {:value "255432"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "255569"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "255669"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "255775"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "255907"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "256048"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "256181"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "256298"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "256418"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "258849"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "307143"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "353580"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19016245"} "2020"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/179"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Kayak Doubles, 500 metres, Women" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "6 –  9 August 2024"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2180"} "National Olympic Nautical Stadium d'Île-de-France, Vaires-sur-Marne, France"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/2008594"} "40 from 16 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The defending Olympic champions were the New Zealand pair of " [:a {:href "/athletes/126097"} "Lisa Carrington"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/131267"} "Caitlin Regal"] ", but Regal was now retired and Carrington had rarely raced K2 since Tokyo. She was entered with a new partner, " [:a {:href "/athletes/145725"} "Alicia Hoskin"] ". Hoskin had won gold at the 2023 World Championships in the K4, with Carrington also in that boat. Hoskin had competed at Tokyo 2020 but did not medal. The German pair of " [:a {:href "/athletes/151240"} "Paulina Paszek"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/143273"} "Jule Hake"] " were world ranked #1 coming into Paris, having won silver at the 2022 World Championships and bronze in 2023."] "\n\n" [:p {} "It was no contest. Carrington and Hoskin were unchallenged in every round, winning the gold medal by over 2 seconds ahead of the Hungarian pair of " [:a {:href "/athletes/130506"} "Tamara Csipes"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/151248"} "Alida Dóra Gazsó"] ", who narrowly edged out Paszek and Hake, and another Hungarian team of " [:a {:href "/athletes/151250"} "Noémi Pupp"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/151251"} "Sára Fojt"] ", as they finished in a rare tie for the bronze medal."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Carrington and Hoskin won gold the day after they had led New Zealand to gold in the K4. Carrington would win a third gold the day after this event in the kayak singles, giving her three gold medals for the second consecutive Olympics. She would leave Paris with nine Olympic medals and eight gold medals. Her eight gold medals equaled the record for the discipline set by German " [:a {:href "/athletes/9879"} "Birgit Fischer-Schmidt"] ", and her nine medals trailed only Fischer-Schmidt’s 12 Olympic medals."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Bib"] [:th {} "